      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Ok another question.&nbsp;</p><p>SubZero has a power that allows him to deal 1 cold damage to 3 non-hero targets. At the end of his turn he must deal x fire damage to himself, where x = the total amount of cold damage he delt this turn. (I think I got that correct)</p><p>He also has an ongoing card that says anytime he takes fire damage he deals that much cold damage to 1 target.&nbsp;</p><p>Doesn&#39;t that set up a loop? Or do we just say the one card&#39;s effect is over so when the second effect comes into play it doesn&#39;t trigger more fire damage to SubZero?</p><p>Thanks!</p>",
